course: dictionary
lesson: 6621
title: Nosy or caring?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nosy means too interested in other people's private business. A nosy person asks too many personal questions or snoops. Look at the clues around the word: «A 4-digit PIN has 10,000 possible codes, from 0000 to 9999, so covering the keypad keeps it secret from nosy people and hidden cameras.» Nosy people are the ones trying to see a secret code, so you must keep them out.
explain: The same kind of question can be nosy or kind. «nín shēntǐ hǎo ma» («neen SHUN-tee HOW mah», literally «is your body well?») means are you keeping well. Asking an elder about health is caring, not nosy. The topic can be the same, so the reason for asking, and whether it is your business, makes the difference.
explain: Before you ask a question, check whether it is your business or their private business. If someone asks you a nosy question, you can answer short and move on. A good friend backs you up.
fact: Nosy means too interested in other people's private business.
fact: A nosy person asks too many personal questions or snoops.
fact: Nosy can also be spelled nosey, and its other forms are nosier and nosiest.
fact: «Nosy parker» is a British phrase for a nosy person.
fact: Being curious about the world is fine; being nosy about other people's diaries, phones or bags is not.
exercise: «A child asked a nosy question about their family.» What makes the question nosy? | *It pokes into private family matters | It asks about the weather | It makes everyone laugh | It has a number in it
exercise: Which question is caring, not nosy? | What is in your private diary? | What is the code for your bag? | Why did you lock your phone? | *Are you keeping well, Grandma?
exercise: Why is a 4-digit PIN kept covered at the keypad? | Because PINs only have two digits | *To keep it secret from nosy people and hidden cameras | To stop the buttons getting dusty | To make the keypad look tidy
test: Which word means too interested in other people's private business? | Shy | *Nosy | Barely | Generous
test: Which of these is a nosy thing to do? | *Read your friend's private diary without asking | Share your crisps at lunch | Say hello to a new classmate | Ask if you can help carry the shopping
exam: A friend is asked a nosy question about their family. What is the best response? | Ask the nosy person about their diary | Ignore the question and cry | *Answer short, move on, and let a good friend back them up | Tell the whole class every private detail
